WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:11.500
<v Product Owner>Thanks for jumping on quickly. I just want to align on scope before the sprint starts — I put the login and signup mock in Figma last night.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Product Owner>To be really clear: for this sprint, we only need the authentication UI built. Just login and signup. Nothing else.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.000
<v Developer>Got it. So not the password-reset flow, and not the account-settings screen that was in the earlier deck?

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Product Owner>Correct, leave those out entirely for now. Password reset is a separate ticket for next sprint. Don't build any of that yet.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Product Owner>The mock has two fields — email and password — a primary Log In button, a "Forgot password?" link, and a line at the bottom for switching to sign up.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:03.000
<v Tester>Should the "Forgot password?" link actually go anywhere yet, or is it just visually present for now?

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Product Owner>Just visually present. It should render, but it doesn't need to be wired to a real flow this sprint — that's part of the next ticket. Same for the sign-up link, it can point to a stub for now.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:26.000
<v Developer>Understood. What should happen on a successful login — where do we route the user?

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:36.000
<v Product Owner>Route to the existing dashboard route, that part already exists. We're only building the login/signup screen and the auth check itself, not anything downstream of it.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:48.000
<v Tester>And validation — do we need inline error messages for a wrong password versus an unrecognized email, or just one generic error?

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:58.000
<v Product Owner>Good question, I don't have a strong opinion — let's flag that as open and decide it during spec review rather than guessing now.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:08.000
<v Developer>Sounds good. I'll treat everything outside login + signup as explicitly out of scope for this ticket, and flag the error-message question as an open item in the spec.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.000
<v Product Owner>Perfect, that's exactly it. Let's get a spec written up from the mock and this conversation, and I'll review it before anyone starts building.
